{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a42b46475f33067e7","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01N6SmmApjc5kwKyFrTWY8wD","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-31072124/-tmp-harvest-translate-m5b650-translated-rust/a9e33088-46e8-41e9-a92d-60a8edf65823/tasks/a42b46475f33067e7.output","summary":"All 54 symbols present, no MISSING. \n\nLet me verify the `PNG_SIZE_MAX` cast in png_check_IHDR handles the width+7 correctly (C casts `width` to png_alloc_size_t before the `&`). My code does `width.wrapping_add(7) as png_alloc_size_t` which computes in u32 first then casts—but C computes `(width + 7)` in png_uint_32 too (unsigned int arithmetic), then `& ~(png_alloc_size_t)7` promotes to size_t. Since width ≤ PNG_UINT_31_MAX passes prior checks but this runs regardless, width+7 could wrap in u32 same as C. This matches. Good.\n\nLet me also double check the `png_get_copyright` and version strings match C's `PNG_STRING_NEWLINE` (\"\\n\") exactly — verified against consts. The translation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated all of `png.c` (libpng 1.6.59) into `/tmp/harvest-translate-m5b650/translated_rust/src/png.rs`.\n\n**All 54 symbols** from `/tmp/symmap/png.txt` are defined and verified present (0 MISSING). This includes:\n- Core: `png_zalloc`, `png_zfree`, `png_reset_crc`, `png_calculate_crc`, `png_create_png_struct`, `png_create_info_struct`, `png_destroy_info_struct`, `png_info_init_3`, `png_data_freer`, `png_free_data`, `png_user_version_check`\n- Version/IO: `png_access_version_number`, `png_get_copyright`, `png_get_libpng_ver`, `png_get_header_ver`, `png_get_header_version`, `png_get_io_ptr`, `png_init_io`, `png_set_sig_bytes`, `png_sig_cmp`, `png_save_int_32`, `png_reset_zstream`, `png_zstream_error`\n- Time: `png_convert_to_rfc1123`, `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer`\n- Colorspace: `png_XYZ_from_xy`, `png_xy_from_XYZ`, `png_muldiv`, `png_reciprocal`, `png_reciprocal2`\n- ICC: `png_icc_check_header`, `png_icc_check_length`, `png_icc_check_tag_table`\n- Gamma: `png_gamma_significant`, `png_gamma_8bit_correct`, `png_gamma_16bit_correct`, `png_gamma_correct`, `png_build_gamma_table`, `png_destroy_gamma_table`\n- Fixed/ASCII: `png_fixed`, `png_fixed_ITU`, `png_ascii_from_fp`, `png_ascii_from_fixed`, `png_check_fp_number`, `png_check_fp_string`\n- Misc: `png_check_IHDR`, `png_build_grayscale_palette`, `png_handle_as_unknown`, `png_chunk_unknown_handling`, `png_set_rgb_coefficients`, `png_set_option`, `png_image_free`, `png_image_error`\n- Data symbols: `png_sRGB_table` [256], `png_sRGB_base` [512], `png_sRGB_delta` [512]\n\n**Key decisions:**\n- Full-feature `pnglibconf.h` with `PNG_FLOATING_ARITHMETIC_SUPPORTED` ON, so I translated the floating-point (double) branches of muldiv/reciprocal/gamma and omitted the fixed-point-only helpers and large lookup tables (`png_8bit_l2`, `png_32bit_exp`, `png_log8bit`, `png_exp`, etc.) that are `#ifdef`-excluded.\n- The three sRGB data tables were verified value-for-value against the C source via script (an initial hand-transcription of `png_sRGB_delta` had extra elements; I regenerated it directly from `png.c` — now exactly 512 and matching).\n- `png_get_uint_32`/`png_save_uint_32`/`png_destroy_read_struct`/`png_destroy_write_struct` are cross-module calls used as ordinary Rust calls per the guide.\n\n**Build status:** `png.rs` has no intrinsic compile errors. The only errors referencing it are 11 unresolved `png_get_uint_32` calls — that function lives in `pngget.rs`, which is still a stub (being filled by other agents), not part of my file's responsibility. All other build errors are located entirely in other stub modules (pngwutil, pngread, pngpread, etc.).","usage":{"total_tokens":236071,"tool_uses":60,"duration_ms":1916033},"uuid":"1ae2035d-08f2-4dd3-a2a4-d1987e5b4355","session_id":"a9e33088-46e8-41e9-a92d-60a8edf65823"}
