{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012s7cVTnfUZ3QrCjDUvwuik","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# libpng → Rust translation conventions (READ FIRST)\n2\t\n3\tYou are translating ONE C source file from `c_src/src/<name>.c` into\n4\t`src/<name>.rs` of a Rust cdylib that reproduces libpng 1.6.59's public ABI\n5\t**byte-for-byte**. The foundation is already written; you only write the\n6\tmodule file.\n7\t\n8\t## Ground rules\n9\t- Do **NOT** modify anything under `c_src/`. Do not touch other `src/*.rs`\n10\t  files, `Cargo.toml`, `build.rs`, `lib.rs`, or the shared modules\n11\t  (`cffi.rs`, `consts.rs`, `helpers.rs`, `pstruct.rs`, `ptypes.rs`).\n12\t- Preserve behaviour EXACTLY, including bugs, order of error checks, integer\n13\t  overflow/wrapping, and rounding. Do not \"improve\" anything.\n14\t- The whole library is built with the full feature set enabled\n15\t  (`pnglibconf.h`). Every `#ifdef` in the C for a feature listed as\n16\t  `#define ..._SUPPORTED` there is ACTIVE; `#undef`/commented ones are OFF\n17\t  (e.g. ARM/NEON/MIPS/SSE/POWERPC/RISCV are OFF; ERROR_NUMBERS OFF;\n18\t  BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS OFF). Translate only the active branches.\n19\t\n20\t## File skeleton\n21\t```rust\n22\t//! Translation of <name>.c\n23\tuse crate::prelude::*;\n24\t```\n25\tThe prelude gives you: all png types (`png_structrp`, `png_bytep`, …), all\n26\tconstants (`PNG_INFO_*`, `png_IDAT`, `PNG_FLAG_*`, …), zlib + libc FFI\n27\t(`malloc`, `memcpy`, `memset`, `fread`, `deflate`, `inflate`, `crc32`,\n28\t`z_stream`, `Z_OK`, …), helper fns (`png_rowbytes`, `png_div257`,\n29\t`png_cstring_from_chunk`, `png_chunk_from_string`, …), and **every other\n30\tlibpng function from every module** (cross-module calls are ordinary Rust\n31\tcalls — just call `png_malloc(png_ptr, n)` etc.).\n32\t\n33\t## Exporting functions\n34\tEvery function that the C file defines with `PNGAPI`/`PNGCBAPI` (exported) OR\n35\tthat is a `PNG_INTERNAL_FUNCTION` (used across files) MUST be:\n36\t```rust\n37\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n38\tpub unsafe extern \"C\" fn png_foo(png_ptr: png_structrp, ...) -> RetType { ... }\n39\t```\n40\tUse the EXACT C signature. Map C types to prelude aliases:\n41\t`png_structrp`→`png_structrp`, `png_bytep`→`png_bytep`,\n42\t`png_const_charp`→`png_const_charp`, `int`→`c_int`, `unsigned int`→`c_uint`,\n43\t`size_t`→`size_t`, `png_uint_32`→`png_uint_32`, `double`→`f64`,\n44\t`voidpf`→`voidpf`, `uInt`→`uInt`. A C function pointer typedef like\n45\t`png_rw_ptr` is `Option<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(...)>` — call via\n46\t`(f.unwrap())(args)` after `f.is_some()`.\n47\t\n48\tFile-`static` (private) C functions become module-private `unsafe fn` (NOT\n49\t`no_mangle`, NOT `pub` required). File-`static` const data becomes `static`.\n50\t\n51\t## Field access\n52\t`png_ptr->field` → `(*png_ptr).field`. All struct fields exist with the same\n53\tnames in `pstruct.rs` (`png_struct_def`, `png_info_def`). Public struct field\n54\tnames match `ptypes.rs`. Callback fields are `Option<fn>`; set with\n55\t`Some(func)` / `None`, test with `.is_some()`, assign a null the C code sets\n56\tvia `= None`.\n57\t\n58\t## Strings\n59\tC string literals → `c\"...\"` C-string literals: `c\"IHDR\".as_ptr()`. Pass\n60\tmessage literals to `png_error(png_ptr, c\"msg\".as_ptr())`.\n61\t\n62\t## Common macros already provided (call as functions)\n63\t- `PNG_ROWBYTES(pixel_bits,width)` → `png_rowbytes(pixel_bits, width)`\n64\t- `PNG_DIV257(v)` → `png_div257(v)`, `PNG_DIV65535` → `png_div65535`\n65\t- `PNG_CSTRING_FROM_CHUNK(s,c)` → `png_cstring_from_chunk(s, c)`\n66\t- `PNG_CHUNK_FROM_STRING(s)` → `png_chunk_from_string(s)`\n67\t- `PNG_STRING_FROM_CHUNK(s,c)` → `png_string_from_chunk(s, c)`\n68\t- chunk id constants: `png_IHDR`, `png_IDAT`, … (u32 values)\n69\t- `PNG_CHUNK_CRITICAL(c)` → `png_chunk_critical(c)` (returns u32 0/1), etc.\n70\t- `png_debug*` macros → drop them (they are no-ops in this build).\n71\t- `PNG_UNUSED(x)` → drop it (or `let _ = x;`).\n72\t- `png_voidcast(type, v)` / `png_constcast(type, v)` / `png_aligncast` →\n73\t  just `v as TargetType` (a Rust cast).\n74\t- `png_sizeof(x)` → `core::mem::size_of::<X>()`.\n75\t\n76\t## zlib\n77\t`png_ptr->zstream` is a real `z_stream` (system zlib). Call `deflate`,\n78\t`inflate`, `deflateReset`, etc. from the prelude. `deflateInit2(&mut zs, ...)`\n79\tand `inflateInit2(&mut zs, wbits)` helper wrappers exist. Return codes:\n80\t`Z_OK`, `Z_STREAM_END`, `Z_BUF_ERROR`, flush values `Z_NO_FLUSH`,\n81\t`Z_FINISH`, etc. `crc32(crc, ptr, len)` available.\n82\t\n83\t## Integer semantics\n84\tUse `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_mul`/`wrapping_shl` or `as`\n85\ttruncation to mirror C wraparound. Right shifts on unsigned are logical.\n86\tCasts between int widths use `as`. Be careful to match C promotion where the\n87\tresult matters.\n88\t\n89\t## Do NOT\n90\t- Do not add `mod` declarations. Do not create helper files.\n91\t- Do not call into the C library. Everything is pure Rust + zlib/libc FFI.\n92\t\n93\t## Verify before finishing\n94\tYour file must define **every** exported symbol the C object exports. The\n95\tlist for your file is in `/tmp/symmap/<name>.txt`. After writing, mentally\n96\tcheck each symbol there has a matching `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern\n97\t\"C\" fn`.\n98\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01CRmHM756dhPRLfoGZ1wxxB","session_id":"a9e33088-46e8-41e9-a92d-60a8edf65823","uuid":"25d41d60-962b-4e65-9f6f-a5c3cac27674","timestamp":"2026-08-05T03:04:53.163Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate pngrutil B1a dispatch"}
